    "q-126178": {
      "dom_id": "step-q126178",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{96}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}-3), & 1\\le x\\le 3 \\\\ 1, & x>3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{96}({2}^{4}+2(2)^{2}-3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{21}{96} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
